### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Success Scenario - Standard Valid Order Request
# Expect: 202 Accepted.
# Verification: Check console logs for Publisher Confirm and successful consumer processing.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Correlation-ID: req-uuid-0001-test

{
  "eventId": "evt_1001",
  "orderId": "ord_9901",
  "amount": 149.99
}

###

### 2. Idempotency Scenario - Duplicate Message Test
# Expect: 202 Accepted by HTTP controller.
# Verification: Consumer will recognize "evt_1001" as already processed and skip processing.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Correlation-ID: req-uuid-0002-test

{
  "eventId": "evt_1001",
  "orderId": "ord_9901",
  "amount": 149.99
}

###

### 3. Business Exception / Retry & DLQ Routing Scenario
# Expect: 202 Accepted initially by HTTP endpoint.
# Verification:
#   1. Consumer will fail due to negative amount.
#   2. Spring AMQP will retry 3 times with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s).
#   3. Message will be routed to Dead Letter Queue (orders.dlq.queue).
#   4. DLQ listener will log the dead-letter alert and x-death reasons.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Correlation-ID: req-uuid-0003-test

{
  "eventId": "evt_1002",
  "orderId": "ord_9902",
  "amount": -50.00
}

###

### 4. Controller-Level Validation Error (Missing Event ID)
# Expect: 400 Bad Request returned directly by @RestControllerAdvice.
# Message will NOT be published to RabbitMQ.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "eventId": "",
  "orderId": "ord_9903",
  "amount": 299.50
}

###

### 5. Controller-Level Validation Error (Null Amount)
# Expect: 400 Bad Request returned directly by @RestControllerAdvice.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "eventId": "evt_1003",
  "orderId": "ord_9904",
  "amount": null
}

###

### 6. High-Value Valid Order Test
# Useful for testing concurrent consumers in parallel
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Correlation-ID: req-uuid-0004-test

{
  "eventId": "evt_1004",
  "orderId": "ord_9905",
  "amount": 1250.00
}

